{
  "dom_id": "step-q249796",
  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "Consider the following geometric sequence:\n\n$$\n-48,\\,36,\\,-27,\\,…\n$$\n\nThe recursive formula for this geometric sequence is\n\n${a}_{n+1}=${{field-1}}$,\\,{a}_{1}=$\n{{field-2}}$,\\,n\\ge 1.$",
  "worked_solution": "The recursive formula for a geometric sequence with common ratio $r$ takes the form\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}=r\\cdot {a}_{n}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, the first term is ${a}_{1}=-48,$ and we can calculate the common ratio $r$ as\n\n$$\nr=\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}}=\\frac{36}{-48}=-\\frac{3}{4}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the recursive formula is\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}=-\\frac{3}{4}{a}_{n},\\,{a}_{1}=-48,\\,n\\ge 1.\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
